# PART 6 — INTERNET IMAGES AND HOTLINKING

IMPORTANT: Use real images from the internet through direct image URLs.

I want the websites to use high-quality photography, not generic colored placeholders.

Use hotlinked images where legally and technically permitted.

Recommended image sources:

- Unsplash
- Pexels
- Wikimedia Commons, where suitable
- Official image sources that explicitly permit embedding

You may use reliable direct image URLs from these sources.

Image requirements:

1. Use relevant images for each industry.
2. Use high-resolution images.
3. Choose images with compositions appropriate to each section.
4. Use different images for different cards.
5. Do not repeat the same image everywhere.
6. Avoid watermarked images.
7. Avoid broken image URLs.
8. Never invent a URL and assume it works.
9. Test each image URL.
10. Add meaningful alt text.
11. Use object-fit: cover where appropriate.
12. Use lazy loading for below-the-fold images.
13. Set image width and height or aspect ratios to prevent layout shifts.
14. Use a suitable background position for each image.
15. Add graceful fallback images or background colors if an external image fails.

Use direct image URLs in HTML or CSS.

Example:

```html
<img
  src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-EXAMPLE"
  alt="Modern residential interior"
  loading="lazy"
>
```

The URL above is only an example format. Do not use a fake image URL.

IMPORTANT IMAGE RULE:

Do not use random images that merely look attractive. Choose images that actually match the section.

For example:

- HVAC: air conditioning units, HVAC technicians, heating and cooling systems, residential homes.
- ATELIER: bespoke suits, tailoring details, luxury fabrics, fashion portraits, sewing craftsmanship.
- DentCare: modern dental clinics, dental consultation, clean treatment rooms, dental professionals.
- EstateFlow: luxury apartments, architecture, modern homes, interior photography, city neighborhoods.
- Main portfolio: relevant screenshots or visual previews of the four websites.

If you cannot verify an external image URL, choose another source or use a clean fallback.

Do not download images unless necessary. Prefer hotlinking to valid direct image URLs.

Respect the source's usage terms and hotlinking restrictions. Do not bypass access controls.

